# Registered here and not in META-INF/spring/*.imports, which is where it was
# first put and where it did nothing. Spring Boot 3 moved auto-configuration to
# `.imports` files but still loads EnvironmentPostProcessors from this file —
# and a misplaced registration is silent: the class compiles, its unit test
# passes, and the running application never calls it.
#
# Found by starting the real jar with a provider set live and reading the
# NoSuchBeanDefinitionException the check exists to replace, after the unit test
# had already passed and been watched failing. See docs/19.
org.springframework.boot.env.EnvironmentPostProcessor=\
tech.bhrigu.almira.provider.ProviderModeCheck
